<section class="mb-5 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-backgroundmd shadow-lg">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-3">Welcome to Project Starter</h1>
  <p>
    You are signed in and ready to build. This placeholder page is where your
    project's main content will go.
  </p>
  <% if (session.authenticatedUser) { %>
    <p class="mt-2 mb-0">
      Signed in as <strong><%= session.authenticatedUser.displayName %></strong>
      <em>(<%= session.authenticatedUser.email %>, role:<%= session.authenticatedUser.role %>)</em>.
    </p>
  <% } %>
</section>

<% if (pageError) { %>
  <%- include("partials/error", { message: pageError }) %>
<% } %>

<section class="max-w-3xl p-6 rounded-2xl bg-backgroundmd shadow-lg">
  <div class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Getting Started</h2>
    <p>
      This starter application provides authentication and role-based authorization
      out of the box. Here are some ideas for where to begin:
    </p>
  </div>

  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
    <li>Replace this page with your project's main dashboard or landing page.</li>
    <li>Add new routes in <code class="bg-textlt/10 px-1 rounded text-sm">src/app.ts</code> and protect them with
      <code class="bg-textlt/10 px-1 rounded text-sm">requireAuthenticated</code> or <code class="bg-textlt/10 px-1 rounded text-sm">requireRole</code>.</li>
    <li>Create new EJS views in <code class="bg-textlt/10 px-1 rounded text-sm">src/views/</code>.</li>
    <li>Add your own models, services, and controllers under <code class="bg-textlt/10 px-1 rounded text-sm">src/</code>.</li>
    <li>Use the Prisma schema in <code class="bg-textlt/10 px-1 rounded text-sm">prisma/schema.prisma</code> to define your database tables.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="max-w-3xl mt-5 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-backgroundmd shadow-lg" x-data="{ open: false }">
  <button
    @click="open = !open"
    class="w-full flex items-center justify-between text-left bg-transparent border-0 p-0 cursor-pointer"
  >
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Alpine.js Demo</h2>
    <span class="text-sm" x-text="open ? 'Hide' : 'Show'">Show</span>
  </button>

  <div x-show="open" x-transition class="mt-4">
    <p class="mb-3">
      Alpine.js is included via CDN and ready to use. This collapsible section is
      a quick demonstration. Use <code class="bg-textlt/10 px-1 rounded text-sm">x-data</code>,
      <code class="bg-textlt/10 px-1 rounded text-sm">x-show</code>,
      <code class="bg-textlt/10 px-1 rounded text-sm">@click</code>, and other
      Alpine directives directly in your EJS templates.
    </p>
    <div x-data="{ count: 0 }" class="flex items-center gap-3">
      <button
        @click="count++"
        class="px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-highlightlt font-medium cursor-pointer hover:bg-highlightlt/80 text-sm"
      >
        Clicked: <span x-text="count">0</span>
      </button>
      <span class="text-sm">A simple Alpine.js counter</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
